{"type":"message","id":"504fabe8","parentId":"997d7c0b","timestamp":"2026-02-11T12:52:47.256Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-11 14:52 GMT+2] Refactor the existing 'seo_logic.php' file into a modular, class-based structure. The goal is to isolate the SEO indicator logic into classes, where each indicator is a self-contained class extending from a parent 'Indicator' abstract class. \n\nRequirements:\n1. Create a parent abstract class 'Indicator' with common methods such as 'analyze()' and shared properties like 'name'.\n2. For each individual SEO indicator (e.g., URL, Meta Data), create a separate class file under 'seo-guides/' directory.\n   - Example: 'UrlIndicator.php', 'MetaIndicator.php'\n3. Each class should override the 'analyze()' method and implement unique logic for its corresponding SEO analysis task.\n4. Refactor 'seo_logic.php' to dynamically load and execute the corresponding SEO class based on the requested indicator.\n\nUse minimum PHP 8 features (strict types, namespaces) to ensure compatibility.\n\nGenerated code will be saved in separate files ('Indicator.php', individual indicator classes, refactored seo_logic.php'). Please ensure code is error-free and suitable for XAMPP/Hostinger environments."}],"timestamp":1770814367253}}
